        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does SpectralLock OCR or invent letters from a black-box redaction?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. SpectralLock leftover container bytes recover honestly (leftover_bytes, recovered_from). Opaque rewrite with nothing left refuses SL-UNREDACT-OPAQUE — never invent letters. Locate / lift / recover / refuse. Inject ON is paint. After spectrallock#13 LIVE (merge 4af8fcb), product Worker GET|POST https://spectrallock-download-tracker.vibelock.workers.dev/v1/unredact is deep PDF + revision_graph + per-revision copies; GET|POST https://spectrallock-download-tracker.vibelock.workers.dev/v1/recover is universal artifact recover (NO-LIE; LIVE vs SLOT); GET|POST https://spectrallock-download-tracker.vibelock.workers.dev/v1/handwriting is physical ink scan heuristics. Never OCR-from-black-box. OCR runs only after structural recovery and never reconstructs covered letters from context. Never OCR-from-black-box. Never claim pigment recovery, ESDA, chemical, lab, or forensic certification. Author Aziel Eliab. NO-LIE. Preview a small overlay on an image; leftover container bytes recover honestly, opaque rewrite refuses. Worker: https://spectrallock-download-tracker.vibelock.workers.dev/ Author Aziel Eliab only. Lamb Lens: Service → Clarity → Peace."
          }
        },
